_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 24
---
order: 24
---
short_label: VIII.24
---
statement: If two numbers have to one another the ratio which a square number has to a square number, and the first is square, then the second is also a square.
---
proof:

Let the two numbers *A* and *B* have to one another the ratio which the square number *C* has to the square number *D,* and let *A* be square.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="190" height="170" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VIII.24 diagram" src="propVIII24.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "VIII.24",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;-1000,40;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;1000,40;0;0",
            "B0;point;free;-1000,75;0;0",
            "B3;point;free;1000,75;0;0",
            "C0;point;free;-1000,110;0;0",
            "C3;point;free;1000,110;0;0",
            "D0;point;free;-1000,145;0;0",
            "D3;point;free;1000,145;0;0",
            "A1;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,30,0;0",
            "A2;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,100,0;0",
            "A;line;connect;A1,A2;black",
            "B1;point;lineSlider;B0,B3,30,0;0",
            "B2;point;lineSlider;B0,B3,160,0;0",
            "B;line;connect;B1,B2;black",
            "C1;point;lineSlider;C0,C3,30,0;0",
            "C2;point;lineSlider;C0,C3,75,0;0",
            "C;line;connect;C1,C2;black",
            "D1;point;lineSlider;D0,D3,30,0;0",
            "D2;point;proportion;A1,A2,B1,B2,C1,C2,D1,D3;0",
            "D;line;connect;D1,D2;black"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

I say that *B* is also square.

Since *C* and *D* are square, *C* and *D* are similar plane numbers. Therefore one mean proportional number falls between *C* and *D.* [!just VIII.18]

And *C* is to *D* as *A* is to *B,* therefore one mean proportional number falls between *A* and *B* also. And *A* is square, therefore *B* is also square. [!just VIII.18; VIII.22]

Therefore, *if two numbers have to one another the ratio which a square number has to a square number, and the first is square, then the second is also a square.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
<br clear="all">
---
body:

The proof of this proposition is straightforward.
